# The kernel sends itself an NMI through the local APIC's ICR. The NMI
# runs on IST2; in this test only, its handler recurses until IST2 runs
# into the unmapped guard page below it. The page fault cannot push its
# frame there, so the CPU raises a double fault, which runs on IST1 and
# reports: an IST overflow ends in the #DF report, not a triple fault.
cmdline: test=nmi_stack
exit: failure
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: nmi_stack: sending an NMI to local APIC 0 through the ICR
expect: nmi_stack: NMI on IST2; recursing until IST2
expect: nmi_stack: double fault with CR2
expect: in IST2's guard page
expect: KERNEL PANIC at kernel/src/arch/x86_64/trap.rs:
expect: DF double fault (vector 8) in ring 0
expect: frame on IST1
